test_matrix -- the matrix file (Nov 2026)
=======================================================================

QUICK START

  sh run_matrix_tests.sh [path-to-del_vor]   7 runs, about 3 s
  open summary.html

WHAT IS TESTED

  del_vor -matrix FILE writes the coefficient matrix for ParaView: one
  point per entry of the .stor matrix at (j, -i, 0) (row 1 at the
  top), both halves and the diagonal, each a VTK vertex cell, with
  point data i, j, area, distance, coefficient, class (0 diagonal, 1
  boundary, 2 interior, 3 interface), negative, zero_area, alpha_min,
  angle, material_i, material_j, volume (manual, section 10, "The
  matrix file"). -matrix_bins N also writes an N x N image (.vti):
  count, negative and min_coefficient per block of rows and columns.

  Each case runs, in work/NAME,
    del_vor -avs MESH -stor NAME.stor -matrix NAME_matrix.vtu
            -paraview NAME -paraview_faces on -report NAME.report ARGS
  (the ParaView files give the checks their alpha and their faces).

WHERE THE ANSWERS COME FROM

  test_paraview's vtu_read.py reads the files (written from VTK's file
  format; check_matrix.py reads the image's header itself). The
  answers come from the .stor of the same run and from the mesh,
  worked out here, never from del_vor's own code:

  entries    one point per .stor entry of the selected rows, in the
             .stor's order, at (j, -i, 0), each a vertex cell
  values     coefficient = A/d of the .stor (which holds -A/d),
             distance from the mesh, area = A/d times d, the diagonal's
             volume = the .stor volume (1e-12 of the largest)
  mirror     (i, j) and (j, i) hold the same values
  class      from the mesh: tets, a face in one tet makes its edges
             boundary, a face between two itetclr interface (interface
             wins); triangles, by the itetclr of the triangles at the
             edge
  flags      negative = A/d < 0; zero_area = |A| <= 1e-12 d^2 (tets),
             1e-12 d (triangles), only with zero_area keep
  material   imt1 read from the mesh file
  alpha      the smallest alpha of the cells around the edge, from
             NAME_mesh.vtu
  angle      tets: from the sum of the edge's dual faces' vector areas
             in NAME_faces.vtu (1e-8 degrees; faces with less than
             1e-6 of the largest area are left out: a tie's face has
             nearly no area and its direction is round-off); triangles
             with Voronoi: 0
  shape      the report's entries, bandwidth and profile equal those of
             the whole .stor
  image      the pixels' count, negative and min_coefficient equal
             those worked out from the points, and the image lies over
             them (origin and spacing)

WHAT WAS FOUND (Nov 14 2026)

  - With acos, the angle of a Voronoi face came out as large as 2e-6
    degrees (acos near 1 loses half the digits); del_vor uses atan2 of
    the cross and dot products: the network's Voronoi angles are now
    at most 6e-12 degrees.
  - A Voronoi face of a negative coefficient has angle 180 degrees: it
    is still perpendicular to its edge, but points backward.

PICTURES (logs/)

  NAME.svg   the matrix, row 1 at the top: black diagonal, blue
             boundary, gray interior, green interface, red negative,
             orange rings zero area; beside it, with matrix_bins, the
             image (color: number of entries, log scale; red: a block
             with a negative entry)

